{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/772745-hunter-the-reckoning-st-tips","id":772745,"title":"Hunter: the Reckoning ST tips","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-23T19:56:07-08:00","id":772745,"title":"Hunter: the Reckoning ST tips","content":"So, I've begun work on an idea which may one day bloom into a full-blown H:tR game. I'm still very much in the preliminary stages, but can anyone offer me any tips on how to run a H:tR game, frequent pitfalls/things to watch out for, general advice? I've run a few games, and they <i>seemed</i> to be reasonably well-received, so while general-ST advice is always appreciated it's not really what I'm looking for here.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T01:59:02-08:00","id":772883,"title":"","content":"Well, the big question is, are you playing with WOD experts, WOD novices, or a mix?<br /> <br /> HtR's generally not such a rough game to run. You get to custom build the monsters to suit your story. You can run it on the grittier side, or the more monster-hunt of the week side without any major tweaks. PCs aren't going to get a large list of powers (13 to 23 maxed out at end game). The biggest things are managing how much Conviction you hand out because that sets the tone for the game more than anything else, and remembering that the Imbued are pretty squishy and have shit healing powers so plan for some downtime esp. if you don't have a Redeemer with Mercy 6 around; unless you want them to regularly start scenes a few HL down.<br /> <br /> My initial question comes in, because HtR not focusing on having the other supernaturals being what they are in their books can really mess with expectations. People that have never really played WOD have no idea what to expect. They're not going to get all frustrated when vampires can walk in the sun without burning up, or humans turn into werewolves if they survive a bite. Experienced WOD players (often completely unintentionally and not maliciously) assume that if you're using a supernatural from one of the major lines, it'll follow those rules rather than use the HtR monster rules. I've seen PCs die because of players making these sorts of assumptions without realizing it. If it might be an issue, bring it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T22:21:49-08:00","id":773650,"title":"","content":"Unsure as to their knowledge of oWoD mechanics and fluff, but safe to say a mix, most likely. My personal knowledge is scattered, so I was going to use what I know and what I can pick up from a loose scan as inspiration, and basically make up the rest. I generally like to have player expectation be not totally wrong, but not totally right either; I've played under STs that have made pretty sweeping changes to prevent players drawing on out-of-character knowledge, and I generally don't enjoy it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T09:09:41-08:00","id":774034,"title":"","content":"ok...if youre still learning DONT USE EITHER THE HERMITS OR THE WAYWARDS!.<br /> <br /> those can be game breaking guys<br /> <br /> <br /> if any of your players is aiming to turn into a wayward, turn him into an avenger. if a hermit is about to be born, make him an spectator or a visionary<br /> <br /> Two: dont worry if your players decide Not to investigate the secret origins of the hunters (i mean the imbueds and such). no one really goes there<br /> <br /> dont go for the Fall from grace unless you want a really though opponent.<br /> <br /> Hunters Die Every Day. Some in epic battles, some others while being mugged. No one lives forever and thats part of the price and the toll that hunters have to deal with<br /> <br /> Everyone is Right and Everyone is Wrong when it comes to The MDG, guys like God45 have too much knowledge but his way of acting might be ethically wrong. while others like BookWorm might be &quot;Betrayers&quot; because of their &quot;Fondness&quot; to the supernatural<br /> <br /> Hunter-Net is a Great Tool for making stories. Some of my best games involved a certain user called Carpenter(Read Hunter the walking dead)<br /> <br /> Have Fun. Happy trails<br /> <br /> and remember, Hunters leave no evidence. in my world at least, if you use certai powers nothing happends. its impossible to collect evidence from a werewolf attack or the remains of a vampire etc... its impossible to find anything out of the ordinary when it comes to investigations from the CSI crew","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T12:46:09-08:00","id":774207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/772745-hunter-the-reckoning-st-tips?p=773650#post773650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unsure as to their knowledge of oWoD mechanics and fluff, but safe to say a mix, most likely. My personal knowledge is scattered, so I was going to use what I know and what I can pick up from a loose scan as inspiration, and basically make up the rest. I generally like to have player expectation be not totally wrong, but not totally right either; I've played under STs that have made pretty sweeping changes to prevent players drawing on out-of-character knowledge, and I generally don't enjoy it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You shouldn't have to make any sweeping changes. In fact, the HtR lines does a lot of work for you in this regard in various supplements. There's a few supplements that are specific to different supernaturals/WOD groups, and they generally do a good job of giving you the tools to make NPCs that fall in line with how normal WOD characters from those groups operate, without having to reach out of HtR's toolbox. <br /> <br /> Even if you never crack open a WtA book, there's enough material in HtR to run werewolf NPCs that should behave like the Garou well enough it isn't a problem.<br /> <br /> My advice is more oriented towards talking to your group about it. Managing expectations works best via talking it out before the game starts, which avoids things like doing massive changes to prevent players from using OOC knowledge from the other games. Find out what they want. If they want you to make monsters without winks and nods to the rest of the WOD so it helps them treat a werewolf like a HtR werewolf not a Garou, do that. If they're cool with you mixing and matching things so you have Camarilla vampires that can go out in the day, but lose all their powers instead of burning up, you can do that too. If they really have trouble separating things, you can use the supplements or other gameline books to run them as-is, and account for things by the nature of the plots you put forward.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/772745-hunter-the-reckoning-st-tips?p=774034#post774034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok...if youre still learning DONT USE EITHER THE HERMITS OR THE WAYWARDS!.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to disagree a bit. Screw PC Waywards though.<br /> <br /> But Hermits are a different thing. The challenges with Hermits aren't really a challenge specific to HtR, but a general GMing/playstyle challenge. Making Hermit PCs work is less game breaking, and more game limiting. You have to find a way to make the Hermit function in the group, so everyone has fun, which is hard with a character type that hates being part of groups that go around interacting with monsters; even to kill them.<br /> <br /> If you've seen the 13 Ghosts remake (the one with Tony Shaloub), Dennis (Matthew Lillard's character) is pretty much a Hermit. He works fine for a movie, but you can imagine how grating that could be every session.<br /> <br /> Hermits are basically the same problem with dealing with any sort of &quot;mission control&quot; style character that wants to hang back from the action and be there to help with information gathering, and long distance support.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hunter-Net is a Great Tool for making stories. Some of my best games involved a certain user called Carpenter(Read Hunter the walking dead) </div> </div> </div>I'd highly recommend giving it an upgrade though. Using a list-serve in 2015 is just weird. There's a lot of stuff with VPNs and such that make a lot more sense for HtR set in the now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T18:28:29-08:00","id":774438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/772745-hunter-the-reckoning-st-tips?p=774207#post774207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to disagree a bit. <b>Screw PC Waywards though</b>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>What makes you say this? I've seen many Waywards played in quite the awesome manner in a number of HtR games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T00:12:55-08:00","id":774577,"title":"","content":"1) It's a thread for a new HtR ST, and Waywards are not newbie friendly. They're mechanics can strongly mess with Conviction flow, narrative flow, and the whole, &quot;I can force the rest of the group to relentless attack the nearest monster and possibly get them killed,&quot; power. It's also very annoying at high end level games where the Wayward ends up with 7 Derangements to another Hunter's 12... despite the Waywards supposedly being the most brokenly insane ones.<br /> <br /> 2) A splat with the default state of, &quot;mass murdering psychopath,&quot; is a giant wrench in group dynamics. It's like playing a Black Spiral Dancer in an otherwise normal Garou pack.<br /> <br /> Yes, I know some people enjoy them. But I've never had a good game with PC ones, and I'm never recommending someone have PC ones in their first run at the game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T11:16:37-08:00","id":774922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/772745-hunter-the-reckoning-st-tips?p=774577#post774577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1)Yes, I know some people enjoy them. But I've never had a good game with PC ones, and I'm never recommending someone have PC ones in their first run at the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good. To each his own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T23:07:43-08:00","id":775279,"title":"","content":"Just thinking about the 'hunter sight' thing, I know normally the Imbued need to spend Conviction to 'see', would making that a constant, always-on thing be a bad house rule? Like it's broken/anti-thematic/whatever?<br /> <br /> Just thinking I kind of like the idea of walking down the street and seeing a corpse pushing a pram, or a demon working a cash register, or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T23:59:05-08:00","id":775295,"title":"","content":"It's kinda broken. It's one of the Wayward's &quot;perks,&quot; though it also drives them insane (and aggressively violently so since they have to take a Derangement like Antisocial PD for it as well). It also messes with Conviction rates, which means it messes with character advancement.<br /> <br /> I definitely don't advise it for the first time with the game. There's a few things to consider beyond that:<br /> <br /> 1) Make sure to read the Second Sight sections thoroughly. It doesn't automatically identify supernatural types. There are Edges for that. You're not going to get, &quot;Demon, risen, vampire, vampire, werewolf, ghost,&quot; like this. You're just going to get, &quot;monster, monster, monster, monster, monster I couldn't see before.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) Imbued can activate the Second Sight reflexively with an Awareness roll. If you want to put the PCs in a situation like this, that's how it should really come up. They get an inkling that a monster is nearby...and they start seeing how many are really around.<br /> <br /> 3) Don't get hung up on this sort of specific situation. It's cool in our heads, but that doesn't make it fun in play. Really wanting something like this to happen all too often ends in railroading the players into it. What does this scene actually add to play? Are you going to have every PC go through this together, or is one getting all this and the rest are oblivious? Does it actually have anything to do with what the PCs are doing?<br /> <br /> If you really want something like this, the best option is to have it be part of a prelude or something similar that's generally not going to be using rolls and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T15:17:44-08:00","id":777390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/772745-hunter-the-reckoning-st-tips?p=775295#post775295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Imbued can activate the Second Sight reflexively with an Awareness roll. If you want to put the PCs in a situation like this, that's how it should really come up. They get an inkling that a monster is nearby...and they start seeing how many are really around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I saw that rule, wasn't 100% on it. So does that work so that the Imbued in question gets a funky feeling or whatever, the player makes the roll. If successful, they can narrow it down to one individual as some non-specific &quot;monster&quot; (needing to use appropriate Edges in order to get a more clear idea, which is when you see them as beast-men, walking corpses, and the like). If not, they're just kind of left feeling funky.<br /> <br /> Is that about right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T15:33:02-08:00","id":777399,"title":"","content":"Second Sight doesn't make them narrow down to a single supernatural if there are multiples around them. Unless those supernaturals are hiding, they'd see any in clear line of sight as being monsters.<br /> <br /> The funky feeling should come after the roll really. They roll to notice the funky feeling. They can activate Second Sight if they succeed and see what's going on, or opt not to, and just be stuck with the funky feeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T17:11:36-08:00","id":777435,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I'm clearly a bit dense: So if they fail the roll, then as far as they're concerned it's all hunky-dory, assuming they don't decide to activate Second Sight for no readily apparent in-character reason? That seems kind of problematic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T20:13:12-08:00","id":777516,"title":"","content":"That is one of the dangers the game presents. If you don't pop on Second Sigh, you're blind to the supernatural that might be around you. So as long as the monsters don't do anything to give you a reason to do it, and your Awareness doesn't kick in, you go on blind to them.<br /> <br /> But that's also why its a &quot;hunt,&quot; the Imbued don't have constantly on &quot;monster-dar,&quot; they have to work to find monsters and save up Second Sight for emergencies, hunches, or when they're sure they're about to deal with something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T04:46:10-08:00","id":777677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/772745-hunter-the-reckoning-st-tips?p=777516#post777516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is one of the dangers the game presents. If you don't pop on Second Sigh, you're blind to the supernatural that might be around you. So as long as the monsters don't do anything to give you a reason to do it, and your Awareness doesn't kick in, you go on blind to them.<br /> <br /> But that's also why its a &quot;hunt,&quot; the Imbued don't have constantly on &quot;monster-dar,&quot; they have to work to find monsters and save up Second Sight for emergencies, hunches, or when they're sure they're about to deal with something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I don't mean problematic as in &quot;power level issues&quot; - the Imbued are meant to be horrendously disadvantaged. I mean problematic from a story perspective - the way I understand things, the Imbued are driven to destroy the monsters; they're <i>wrong</i> in a way that a non-Imbued can't easily understand. But if they aren't aware of a monster, wouldn't that by necessity take at least some wind out of their sails?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T13:54:10-08:00","id":777903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/772745-hunter-the-reckoning-st-tips?p=777677#post777677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean problematic from a story perspective - the way I understand things, the Imbued are driven to destroy the monsters; they're <i>wrong</i> in a way that a non-Imbued can't easily understand. But if they aren't aware of a monster, wouldn't that by necessity take at least some wind out of their sails?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I wouldn't say the &quot;driven to destroy,&quot; that's mostly a Zeal/Avenger mentality.<br /> <br /> They're meant to <i>do</i> something about monsters. Mercy Creeds, and Visionaries are especially more likely to want to &quot;solve&quot; monsters instead of destroy them.<br /> <br /> A lot of the Imbued would say with so many monsters in the world, worrying about the ones keeping their heads down, and not causing trouble is a waste of time. Deal with the outbreak of zombies, over the ghost that's just hanging around its living family harmlessly. Defenders, Judges, Visionaries, and Martyrs are all generally going to attract characters that are in more of a &quot;triage&quot; mentality regarding monsters. Defenders aren't going looking for trouble, they're out to protect people from threats. Most Judges are out to judge monsters, which often means having a bar that some monsters can get under to avoid the Judge's wrathful punishments. etc.<br /> <br /> And yeah... as ST advice, I wouldn't have &quot;make your Awareness check or miss the plot,&quot; be a thing. Make sure there are clues about the central monsters in you plot that don't stall like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}